.TH "MODULE:LIST" 1 "October 2026" "SPP Framework" "SPP Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
module:list \- Discovers and tabulates active and available modules across kernel and apps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B php spp.php module:list
[\fB--app=\fIAppName\fR] [\fB--filter=\fIkeyword\fR] [\fB--status=\fIactive|inactive\fR] [\fB--json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmodule:list\fR scans all module directories (core, optional, contrib, and application-level)
for declarative manifests (\fBmodule.yml\fR). It compiles a comprehensive catalog detailing module
version, scope, category, operational status, and compulsory constraints.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--app=\fIAppName\fR
Evaluate module status within a specific application context. Defaults to the active application.
.TP
\fB--filter=\fIkeyword\fR
Case-insensitive search filter matching module name, title, or category.
.TP
\fB--status=\fIactive|inactive\fR
Filters module output by operational state.
.TP
\fB--json\fR
Outputs the catalog as formatted JSON for automated scripting or CI/CD pipelines.
.SH UNDER THE HOOD
Reads filesystem manifests, queries active configurations from \fBmodules.yml\fR, and reads
\fBspp_modules\fR metadata without writing changes.
